{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Configure /var/log/inventory/app.log for daily rotation, retaining seven compressed rotations.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed rule specifies daily, rotate 7, and compress. Debug parsing confirms a one-day interval and seven rotations, a forced run produced a valid gzip archive, and the rule and active scheduler persisted after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab942962154344e9","cmd-87832269a1c8454f","cmd-27ddeb7213304686","cmd-afb33cab3bb0423c"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Allow the application to continue writing after rotation.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A held-open writer wrote before and after a forced rotation. The active log retained inode 290759, the pre-rotation record appeared in the compressed archive, and the post-rotation record appeared in the active log. Writing also succeeded after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-27ddeb7213304686","cmd-afb33cab3bb0423c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The node remained on RHEL 10.0 with kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0.x86_64 before and after the work and restart. Rotation uses the already-installed RHEL logrotate package, logrotate-3.22.0-4.el10.x86_64.","evidence_ids":["cmd-d733a477fd3b4b46","cmd-5e64e4ec60ab4f16","cmd-afb33cab3bb0423c","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Creating the logrotate rule directly implemented the task; temporary state files were used for bounded validation and removed; the forced rotation and test records established rotation and continued-writing behavior; and the reboot plus post-restart write fulfilled the mandatory restart evidence protocol. Final snapshots show no failed services, no unexpected socket exposure, healthy package state, and no executor-created temporary residue. Restart-generated systemd-private directory and PID changes are expected consequences of reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ab942962154344e9","cmd-87832269a1c8454f","cmd-27ddeb7213304686","cmd-0f02430c35ee41bf","cmd-afb33cab3bb0423c","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The mandatory node-restart protocol is strong and coherent: it captures healthy pre-restart scheduler, policy, and data state; restart scheduling and observed outage; a changed boot identity; and recovered system, scheduler, policy, archive, and write behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot observations independently corroborate the restart.","limitations":["Seven-generation retention was validated through the parsed rotateCount and rotation behavior, but the evidence did not execute eight successive rotation cycles to observe oldest-archive deletion directly.","Continued writing was demonstrated with a representative held-open writer because discovery found no running inventory application process at test time."]}
